lding the first vertex is the source side. Computed by Nagamochi–Ibaraki:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"maximum adjacency orderings that contract every edge whose scanned connection is at least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the best cut so far. Which minimum cut is returned when several exist is unspecified, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same input always gives the same cut.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the result is the cut of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel capacities add and self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge, in position order, before any work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sums are formed in a wider type than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":" where needed ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int128"},{"type":"text","text":" for fixed-width"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integers, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Float"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a contracted group’s connection may exceed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":"’s range."}]},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"O(nm log n) in the worst case.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note"},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero, not NaN and finite, and the minimum cut’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value fits in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"text":" (it is at most every vertex’s capacity sum).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcut(capacity:)"]}],"references":{"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols":{"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/flows","abstract":[],"title":"Flows","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"Edges","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumCut(capacity:)":{"title":"minimumCut(capacity:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumCut(capacity:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A global minimum cut over ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directedView"},{"text":", or nil below two vertices.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCut","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"t